# The nightly usage archive's own needs (#1923 - Move each closed month's
# unlinked usage rows out of Postgres into a Parquet file in a private R2
# bucket). Installed by .github/workflows/analytics-rollup.yml's archive step,
# and on the maintainer's machine for `scripts/analytics_keys.py open` on an
# archived month - never by the API's image, which installs requirements.txt
# alone. requirements.in keeps this backend to one database driver and no
# analytics engine, and the archive is the one job that writes a file format
# the API never reads.
-r requirements.in

# Writes each part (scripts/analytics_archive.py) and reads it back for
# `open`: zstd Parquet, typed from the `analytics_events` model, with no
# extension downloaded at run time - which DuckDB's httpfs would have needed.
pyarrow
